WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.042 --> 00:00:01.919
I would never have gotten into acting

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:05.631
if it wasn't something like
the kid with the prosthetic.

00:00:07.758 --> 00:00:09.134
Who here wants to be on camera?

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:11.929
So you never had been an actor before,

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:13.931
you never necessarily
had an interest in acting.

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:17.518
What was it about this show that you said,
"Yeah, that's like a thing I'd wanna do?"

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:19.436
Just to spread awareness.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.104
It's a great way to inform people.

00:00:21.188 --> 00:00:22.773
I guess that makes sense.

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:25.901
We have episodes
that are about Josh's prosthetic,

00:00:25.984 --> 00:00:27.402
about it breaking
or about him adapting.

00:00:27.486 --> 00:00:29.780
In some ways,
I'm most proud of our episodes

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:30.948
where it's, like, barely mentioned.

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:32.449
Right? He plays soccer.

00:00:32.533 --> 00:00:34.243
He's very enthusiastic. Right?

00:00:34.326 --> 00:00:35.744
He reads a lot of self-help books.

00:00:35.827 --> 00:00:36.662
And he has one leg.

00:00:36.745 --> 00:00:37.955
And he has one leg.

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.373
Uh, guys, listen...

00:00:39.456 --> 00:00:42.960
I wanna make friends because they like me,
not because they feel bad for me.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:44.837
Hey guys, it's Logan Marmino,

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.005
and the great thing about this show,
and the crew,

00:00:47.089 --> 00:00:50.342
is that there are so many different voices
that represent everybody.

00:00:50.425 --> 00:00:52.636
So... why don't we
go meet some of those people?

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.096
This is Miss Nandi.

00:00:54.179 --> 00:00:56.223
One of the First ADs.

00:00:56.932 --> 00:00:58.600
I'm Reggie Junior-Junior.

00:00:58.684 --> 00:00:59.726
And who am I?

00:01:00.018 --> 00:01:02.062
-You're Romy Senior-Senior.
-That's right.

00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:05.190
Yo Yo, what is your job like,
and what do you do?

00:01:05.274 --> 00:01:07.651
I put watches on them.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.903
I put things in people's hands.

00:01:09.987 --> 00:01:11.655
-Pretty cool job.
-Thanks.

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:16.410
I'd like to introduce you to Kiah,
our Production Accessibility Coordinator.

00:01:16.493 --> 00:01:19.997
Yeah, so as the PAC,
I do a lot of stuff that's sort of like...

00:01:20.372 --> 00:01:22.791
disability and accessibility together.

00:01:22.875 --> 00:01:26.170
I get to hang out with Josh and you a lot
when we're doing things

00:01:26.253 --> 00:01:28.839
that are leg involved or crutch involved.

00:01:29.298 --> 00:01:31.216
Do you wanna see the sensory room?

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:34.094
I always wanna be in the sensory fun room.
-Aw yeah, then let’s go.

00:01:34.428 --> 00:01:36.471
If you've got a headache,
you can hang out up here.

00:01:36.555 --> 00:01:40.475
If you have sensory issues,
and you need a place with low light

00:01:40.559 --> 00:01:43.145
and not a lot of sound,
all that's up here.

00:01:43.228 --> 00:01:44.646
That's so cool.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:46.815
Uh, well, I think they're calling me
back down to set.

00:01:46.899 --> 00:01:48.650
-All right, go for it.
-Bye.

00:01:49.484 --> 00:01:53.197
So, today on set we are doing
the Halloween showcase scene,

00:01:53.822 --> 00:01:56.283
and they're actually
doing it right now, behind me.

00:01:57.242 --> 00:02:00.621
And this is my gingerbread man costume.

00:02:01.038 --> 00:02:03.290
Run, run, run, as fast as I can.

00:02:03.373 --> 00:02:06.084
You can't catch me,
I'm the gingerbread man.

00:02:09.087 --> 00:02:11.298
Somebody grab me a doctor!

00:02:11.465 --> 00:02:13.926
Or a least a glass of milk!

00:02:15.511 --> 00:02:21.725
I love the scene where Josh gets to feel
like he can go to school without a leg on,

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.852
and everybody was, like, cheering for him.

00:02:23.936 --> 00:02:25.145
That was awesome!

00:02:25.229 --> 00:02:29.274
The first scene
that I got to do in episode 6,

00:02:29.358 --> 00:02:32.194
Josh's leg has broken at Halloween.

00:02:32.528 --> 00:02:35.072
I wrote most of that scene
myself, personally.

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:38.200
And what an amazing experience it was,

00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:44.915
to write a scene that I was gonna perform,
talking to, basically my younger self.

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:48.669
I used to never leave my house
without a prosthesis on.

00:02:48.752 --> 00:02:51.588
I didn't go in public without one
until after college.

00:02:51.672 --> 00:02:54.842
Being able to shoot that scene
in a moment in Josh the character's life,

00:02:54.925 --> 00:02:57.469
when he's so vulnerable, on Halloween,

00:02:57.553 --> 00:03:00.055
was so intense and meaningful
and emotional.

00:03:00.138 --> 00:03:02.474
And it's given me
an even deeper appreciation

00:03:02.558 --> 00:03:04.434
of all the elements and all the people

00:03:04.518 --> 00:03:07.062
that it takes to make a show
like this happen.

00:03:07.145 --> 00:03:07.855
All right, bring it in.

00:03:08.272 --> 00:03:09.273
Let's hear it.

00:03:09.648 --> 00:03:12.317
-Go... Pirates!
-Go... Pirates!

00:03:12.401 --> 00:03:13.777
-Yeah!
-He-Yarrr!

00:03:14.528 --> 00:03:16.530
Thanks for watching,
and I hope you enjoy.

